---
import EditorialPage from '../components/EditorialPage.astro';

const page = {
  path: '/website-migration-services/',
  title: 'Website Migration SEO Services Philippines | Bright Forge',
  description: 'Moving domain, platform or design? We map every URL, write the redirects, test the staging site and monitor search after launch. Based in Quezon City.',
  h1: 'Website Migration SEO Services',
  crumb: 'Website migration',
  lead: [
    'A redesign, a change of CMS or a new domain can cost a site much of its search traffic if the old URLs, redirects and page content are not carried across properly. We plan that part of the move, test it before launch and watch the results afterwards.',
    'Bring us in before the navigation, templates and URL structure are final. After launch we can still help, but repairs cost more than prevention.',
    'We have done this for ourselves: we moved this website from brightforgeseo.com to brightforge.com.ph.',
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      h2: 'What you receive',
      html: `<dl class="bf-deliverables">
<dt>Risk review</dt><dd>What could go wrong on this particular move, in order of seriousness.</dd>
<dt>URL inventory</dt><dd>Every existing URL with its traffic, rankings and links, so nothing valuable is forgotten.</dd>
<dt>Redirect map</dt><dd>Each old URL matched to its closest new page, ready for your developer to implement.</dd>
<dt>Staging review</dt><dd>Titles, headings, canonicals, indexing rules, internal links, structured data and tracking checked on the test site.</dd>
<dt>Launch-day checklist</dt><dd>The checks to run in the first hour, and who runs each.</dd>
<dt>Post-launch monitoring</dt><dd>A crawl of the live site, Search Console checks and a written summary of anything that needs fixing.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Our <a href="/blog/website-migration-seo-checklist/">website migration SEO checklist</a> shows the checks in more detail.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'How we do it, step by step',
      html: `<ol class="bf-steps">
<li><strong>Baseline.</strong> Crawl the current site and export Search Console and analytics data. Where the site has not been reviewed recently, this starts with an <a href="/seo-audit-services/">SEO audit</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Map.</strong> Match old URLs to new ones. Pages with no equivalent are discussed, not silently dropped.</li>
<li><strong>Test.</strong> Review the staging site against the map and the current site.</li>
<li><strong>Agree the controls.</strong> One named person on your side approves the release. We agree in advance which redirect exceptions are acceptable and how tracking will be confirmed.</li>
<li><strong>Launch.</strong> Run the checklist together.</li>
<li><strong>Monitor.</strong> Close checks straight after launch, then at the intervals agreed in the proposal.</li>
</ol>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Moves we cover',
      html: `<p>Redesigns on the same domain, CMS changes (for example WordPress to Astro or Shopify), domain changes, ecommerce replatforming, URL restructures, and merging several sites into one. Where the move includes a rebuild, our <a href="/development/">web design and development</a> team can do the build, and <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO</a> follows through on the fixes.</p>`,
    },
    {
      h2: 'Timeframe and pricing',
      html: `<p>Tell us the launch date as early as you can: the redirect map and staging review have to be finished before it. Each migration is quoted in a written proposal, and the scope depends on the number of URLs and templates.</p>`,
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { question: 'Will we lose traffic?', answer: 'A short dip is common even when everything is done well. The aim is to keep it small and brief. We cannot promise there will be none.' },
    { question: 'Our site has already launched and traffic has fallen. Can you help?', answer: 'Yes. We compare the old and new sites, find what was lost and list the repairs in priority order.' },
    { question: 'Do you work with our developer?', answer: 'Yes. Everything we produce is written to be implemented by a developer, yours or ours.' },
  ],
  contact: { h2: 'Planning a move? Request an SEO review', text: 'Send the current site, the planned launch date and what is changing. We usually reply within one business day.' },
